@.str = private unnamed_addr constant [3923 x i8] c"Most commonly-used cvc5 options:\0A  --incremental | -i     enable incremental solving [*]\0A  --lang=LANG | --input-language=LANG | -L LANG\0A                         force input language (default is \22auto\22; see --lang\0A                         help)\0A  --output=TAG | -o TAG  Enable output tag.\0A  --parse-only           exit after parsing input [*]\0A  --preprocess-only      exit after preprocessing input [*]\0A  --quiet | -q           decrease verbosity (may be repeated)\0A  --rlimit=N             set resource limit\0A  --rlimit-per=N | --reproducible-resource-limit=N\0A                         set resource limit per query\0A  --stats                give statistics on exit [*]\0A  --stats-all            print unchanged (defaulted) statistics as well [*]\0A  --stats-internal       print internal (non-public) statistics as well [*]\0A  --tlimit=MS            set time limit in milliseconds of wall clock time\0A  --tlimit-per=MS        set time limit per query in milliseconds\0A  --verbose | -v         increase verbosity (may be repeated)\0A  --verbosity=N          the verbosity level of cvc5\0A  --decision=MODE | --decision-mode=MODE\0A                         choose decision mode, see --decision=help\0A  --copyright            show cvc5 copyright information\0A  --help | -h            full command line reference\0A  --help-regular | -H    regular command line reference\0A  --interactive          force interactive shell/non-interactive mode [*]\0A  --print-success        print the \22success\22 output required of SMT-LIBv2 [*]\0A  --seed=N | --random-seed=N | -s N\0A                         seed for random number generator\0A  --show-config          show cvc5 static configuration\0A  --version | -V         identify this cvc5 binary\0A  --force-logic=LOGIC    set the logic, and override all further user attempts\0A                         to change it\0A  --strict-parsing       be less tolerant of non-conforming inputs, this is an\0A                         alias for --parsing-mode=strict [*]\0A  --dag-thresh=N         dagify common subexprs appearing > N times (1 ==\0A                         default, 0 == don't dagify)\0A  --expr-depth=N         print exprs to depth N (0 == default, -1 == no limit)\0A  --output-lang=LANG | --output-language=LANG\0A                         force output language (default is \22auto\22; see\0A                         --output-lang help)\0A  --proof-granularity=MODE\0A                         modes for proof granularity\0A  --enum-inst            enumerative instantiation: instantiate with ground\0A                         terms from relevant domain, then arbitrary ground terms\0A                         before answering unknown [*]\0A  --full-saturate-quant  resort to full effort techniques instead of answering\0A                         unknown due to limited quantifier reasoning. Currently\0A                         enables enumerative instantiation [*]\0A  --print-inst=MODE      print format for printing instantiations\0A  --check-models         after SAT/INVALID/UNKNOWN, check that the generated\0A                         model satisfies user assertions [*]\0A  --check-proofs         after UNSAT/VALID, check the generated proof (with\0A                         proof) [*]\0A  --check-unsat-cores    after UNSAT/VALID, produce and check an unsat core\0A                         (expensive) [*]\0A  --produce-models | -m  support the get-value and get-model commands [*]\0A  --produce-proofs       produce proofs, support check-proofs and get-proof [*]\0A  --produce-unsat-cores  turn on unsat core generation. Unless otherwise\0A                         specified, cores will be produced using SAT soving\0A                         under assumptions and preprocessing proofs. [*]\0A  --condense-function-values\0A                         condense values for functions in models rather than\0A                         explicitly representing them [*]\0A  --default-function-value-mode=MODE\0A                         mode for choosing default values for functions\0A\00", align 1
